From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] healthd: use the discovered battery for lockscreen charging
 info

"core: Lockscreen Charging (2/3)" computes maxChargingCurrent and
maxChargingVoltage from /sys/class/power_supply/battery/current_now and
voltage_now, and falls back to the charger's own current_now and
voltage_now when that power supply is missing. Batteries are not always
named "battery": on the Huawei MateBook E Go it is gaokun-ec-battery. The
chargers there are an adapter supply without current_now/voltage_now and a
UCSI supply that reports 0 for both under a USB PD contract. With a PD
charger both values are therefore 0, and SystemUI shows a default of 5 V
without current or wattage on the lockscreen.

When there is no "battery" power supply, read the current and voltage of
the battery device BatteryMonitor has already discovered, the one the rest
of HealthInfo comes from, and fall back to the charger only when that
device does not provide them. This follows the existing preference for
battery values: on devices without a "battery" supply whose chargers do
report current_now and voltage_now, the lockscreen now shows the
battery's values instead of the charger's. Devices with a power supply
named "battery" behave as before.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp    | 9 ++++++++-
 healthd/BatteryMonitor_v1.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp b/healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp
index 0daf4b5..074a61d 100644
--- a/healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp
+++ b/healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp
@@ -608,9 +608,13 @@ void BatteryMonitor::updateValues(void) {
             int ChargingCurrent = 0;
             int ChargingVoltage = 0;
 
-            // Prefer battery current_now / voltage_now
+            // Prefer battery current_now / voltage_now. Without a power supply
+            // named "battery", use the battery device found by the scan above.
             if (access(SYSFS_BATTERY_CURRENT, R_OK) == 0) {
                 ChargingCurrent = abs(tryGetIntField(String8(SYSFS_BATTERY_CURRENT)).value_or(0));
+            } else if (!mHealthdConfig->batteryCurrentNowPath.empty()) {
+                ChargingCurrent =
+                        abs(tryGetIntField(mHealthdConfig->batteryCurrentNowPath).value_or(0));
             } else {
                 path.clear();
                 path.appendFormat("%s/%s/current_now", POWER_SUPPLY_SYSFS_PATH,
@@ -622,6 +626,9 @@ void BatteryMonitor::updateValues(void) {
 
             if (access(SYSFS_BATTERY_VOLTAGE, R_OK) == 0) {
                 ChargingVoltage = abs(tryGetIntField(String8(SYSFS_BATTERY_VOLTAGE)).value_or(0));
+            } else if (!mHealthdConfig->batteryVoltagePath.empty()) {
+                ChargingVoltage =
+                        abs(tryGetIntField(mHealthdConfig->batteryVoltagePath).value_or(0));
             } else {
                 path.clear();
                 path.appendFormat("%s/%s/voltage_now", POWER_SUPPLY_SYSFS_PATH,
